## Example local.properties file for Face Filter Android Studio project
## Copy this file to "local.properties" and update the paths for your system

## Android SDK path
## macOS: /Users/username/Library/Android/sdk
## Linux: /home/username/Android/Sdk
## Windows: C:/Users/username/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk
sdk.dir=/Users/username/Library/Android/sdk

## Android NDK path (MUST use r17c or r18b - r19+ not supported)
## macOS: /Users/username/Library/Android/sdk/ndk/r18b
## Linux: /home/username/Android/Sdk/ndk/r18b
## Windows: C:/Users/username/AppData/Local/Android/Sdk/ndk/r18b
ndk.dir=/Users/username/Library/Android/sdk/ndk/r18b

## CMake path (version 3.9.2 or higher required)
## macOS (Homebrew): /usr/local
## Linux: /usr or /usr/local
## Windows: C:/Program Files/CMake
cmake.dir=/usr/local

## Notes:
## 1. Replace "username" with your actual username
## 2. Use forward slashes (/) or escaped backslashes (\\) for Windows paths
## 3. Ensure cmake.dir points to directory containing bin/cmake executable
## 4. NDK r19 and higher are NOT supported due to structural changes
## 5. You can check your paths:
##    - Android Studio → Preferences → Appearance & Behavior → System Settings → Android SDK
##    - Run: which cmake (macOS/Linux) or where cmake (Windows)
